course: dictionary
lesson: 11545
title: Amended: changed to make it better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Amended is a word about change. When something is amended, someone has changed it a little to fix it or make it better. «The class amended the rules for the playground game, so everyone could take a turn.» The rules were not thrown away. A few parts were changed to make them fairer.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Our timetable was amended because the swimming lesson moved to Friday.» The reason is given, and only one part changed, so amended means changed a little. Try the check: swap in "changed a little". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Amended is also the past tense of the verb amend, so you may also see amend, amends and amending. A first version is still the starting point, and the amended version has small changes to it.
fact: Amended means changed a little to correct or improve something.
fact: Amend is the verb, and amended is its past tense, as in «She amended her story».
fact: Amended is often used for rules, laws, plans and timetables.
fact: An «amended version» is a newer version with small changes to the first one.
fact: Amended is not the same as new: the first version is changed, not thrown away.
exercise: «The class amended the rules for the playground game.» What does amended mean here? | Written down for the first time | Thrown away completely | *Changed a little to make them fairer | Read out loud to the class
exercise: «Our timetable was amended because the swimming lesson moved to Friday.» What changed? | *The swimming lesson moved to Friday | Nothing changed at all | The whole school closed for a year | The timetable was thrown in the bin
exercise: Find and copy the word in «She amended her story after her teacher pointed out the mistakes.» that means changed to improve it. | teacher | mistakes | story | *amended
test: «The new law was amended to protect the park.» What does amended mean here? | Ruined | Cleaned | *Changed a little to improve it | Cancelled for ever
test: Which word is the verb that amended comes from? | ambled | amazed | amuse | *amend
exam: «The recipe was amended: less sugar, more fruit.» What does amended mean here? | *Changed a little to make it better | Read aloud | Thrown away | Made longer
